VNA Hanoi - VNA correspondents reported that on the morning of February 11, Vietnamese Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh and his wife visited the University of Brunei Darussalam (UBD, short for "Brunei Darussalam University") during their visit to Brunei Darussalam.
The University of Brunei Darussalam is the largest higher education and scientific research center in Brunei, ranking third in the regional university rankings.
Universiti Brunei Darussalam is one of the symbols of Vietnam and Brunei’s cooperation in education and training.
The University of Brunei Darussalam officially established a cooperation relationship with Vietnam's FPT University in July 2013, mainly in the field of English training.
In addition to foreign languages such as English, French, German, Japanese and Korean, Brunei University also incorporates Vietnamese into its curriculum.
During the visit to Brunei University, the Prime Minister of the Government of Vietnam, Ms. Fan Minh Diem, and Ms. Nguyen Phu Trong held a discussion with students of the Vietnamese language class.
Prime Minister Fan Minh Diệm is pleased that more and more foreigners are interested in learning Vietnamese and are making a positive contribution to promoting Vietnamese cultural characteristics and the image of Vietnamese people around the world.
Prime Minister Fan Mingzheng expressed his belief and hope that the Vietnamese language teaching staff at the University of Brunei will become increasingly strong; students in the Vietnamese class are becoming more interested in Vietnamese, working hard to learn it well, so they can use fluent Vietnamese soon and be ambassadors for friendly relations between the two countries.
Prime Minister Fan Minh Diem also took the opportunity to speak via video with Vietnamese students studying English at FPT-UBD Global Centre in Phnom Penh, to learn about their learning, especially during the pandemic.
Prime Minister Fan Minh Diem said the cooperation between FPT University of Vietnam and Brunei University, especially the FPT-UBD Global Centre, is a living symbol of the educational cooperation between Vietnam and Brunei.
The students of the center are also hoping to make greater progress in their studies and make a positive contribution to the friendly and cooperative relations between the two countries.
In his discussions with the Minister of Education and the leadership of Brunei University, Prime Minister Fan Ming-jiang highly praised the achievements of the two countries in educational cooperation, including the cooperation between FPT University and Brunei University, and the initiative of Brunei University to include Vietnamese in the curriculum.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh hoped that the University of Brunei Darussalam would continue to pay attention to ensuring the quality of Vietnamese language teaching and expand the scale of Vietnamese language classes.
Prime Minister Fan Minh Minh also highly appreciated the positive results of the cooperation between the two countries based on the Memorandum of Understanding on Education Cooperation signed in April 2014 and recommended that Brunei continue to provide more scholarships and to effectively implement short-term exchange training projects such as the Global Discovery Programme and the Discovery Year.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh highly praised the establishment of the first branch of the University of Brunei in Vietnam in Southeast Asia; believing that the university will grow in scale in the region and the world; and further expanding cooperation with Vietnamese higher education institutions.
During this opportunity, Premier Feng Mingzheng and his wife planted memorial trees on the campus of the University of Brunei Darussalam, and left messages on the memorial book.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh wished that the University of Brunei Darussalam would continue to develop and contribute more and more to the education sector of Brunei. He also hoped that the cooperation between Vietnamese education and training institutions and Brunei would become more extensive and deeper.
(Complete)
