Several indicators of decline in Taiwan's economy in the first quarter of the year - China News
Xinhua News Agency, Taipei, February 11 (reported by Zhao Bo and Huang Yang) - The export trade volume "连五黑" and the manufacturing purchasing managers index (PMI) have been contracting for seven consecutive months, and the consumer price index (CPI) has seen "3-digit" again... Recently, the Taiwan authority released the economic data of January 2023.
Experts analyzed that the performance of the Taiwanese economy at the beginning of the year was not good, and the growth pressure was not small.
According to the Ministry of Finance of Taiwan’s Treasury Affairs Bureau, Taiwan’s exports for January this year amounted to $31.51 billion, down 21.2% from last year and marking their fifth consecutive month of negative growth.
The export value of 11 major export commodities fell year-on-year in the same period.
Plastic rubber and its products, as well as optical instruments, had the sharpest declines of 37.6% and 35.7%, respectively.
The export of electronic components fell by 20.1% year-on-year, the largest decline in 11 years.
Among them, the annual decline of integrated circuits was 18.3%, the biggest decline in 14 years.
According to the department's statistics director, Ms. Kimena, this shows that the effects of weak demand in the consumer electronics industry are spreading and the electronics industry is entering a correction period.
Statistics show that imports and exports from Taiwan doubled in January, with a surplus of only $2.34 billion, the lowest level in almost three years.
The Taiwan authorities’ finance bureau believes that global terminal demand is declining, industrial adjustments in inventory will suppress manufacturers' purchasing intentions for materials, and export weakness may not improve temporarily. The Taiwanese first-quarter exports could be worse than expected this year.
According to the Taiwan Institute of Economic Research, in January this year, the Purchasing Managers’ Index (PMI) for manufacturing in Taiwan was revised down from 46.8% to 40.4%, with a decline of 3.3 percentage points compared to December last year and its seventh consecutive contraction.
In the economic monitoring index system, PMI is at 50% as the turning point for health and illness; an index greater than 50% indicates expansion of prosperity, while less than 50% signifies contraction.
In January, the five components of the PMI in Taiwan were tightened, including new orders, production and employment, and the delivery time of suppliers was shortened, and the inventory was tightened.
All six industries have returned a PMI contraction, and the order of contraction is as follows: the electricity and machinery industry (35.1%), the electronic and optical industry (35.2%), the chemical and biotechnology industry (39.2%), the basic raw materials industry (42.4%), the transportation industry (42.6%) and the food and textile industry (45.7%).
On the price side, the Directorate-General of Budget, Accounting and Statistics of the Executive Yuan announced that the CPI of Taiwan in January was 3.04%, which was higher than 3% for the second time since July last year.
Among them, the price of vegetables rose by 28.25%, which was a 17-month high.
The special member of the Executive Yuan of Taiwan, Cao Zhigang, admitted that the increase in vegetable prices exceeded expectations. Excluding the factor of the Spring Festival, the average CPI in January and February of this year should be close to 2.71% in December of last year, and the inflation pressure is still there, and it is still at a high point.
Looking forward to the Taiwanese economy this year, the overall reports of the Taiwanese media, including the United Report and Yahoo Finance, are pessimistic.
Wu Da-ren, a professor of the Department of Economics at the Central University of Taiwan, analyzed that the export slump may cause the cash flow of export manufacturers to be problematic, and the default risk will increase.
At the same time, the decrease in orders leads to manufacturers cutting human costs, affecting the labor market and household economy, which in turn impacts the consumption capacity.
Chiou Tsa-sheng, a researcher at the Institute of Taiwanese Economic Research, believes that the inflationary situation in Europe and the United States has not been resolved, and the demand continues to shrink. He predicts that the export decline in Taiwan will continue until the first half of the year.
The full-year growth performance will be lower than last year, as Taiwan's economy is supported by exports and is affected by the decline in exports.
The balloon incident sharpened the eyes of the United States?
Strengthening restrictions on technology exports to China
The Wall Street Journal reported today that the United States is preparing to further tighten its technology exports to China after the balloon incident.
The current and former security officials said the balloon incident highlighted the national security threat posed by China and would help to win more political support for strengthening U.S. technology protection.
The US claims that the balloon carried antennas and sensors for intelligence gathering and communications.
According to Martijn Rasser, a senior official of the former US Central Intelligence Agency and now serving at the New American Security Center in Washington, D.C.
This is undoubtedly fueling the fire of hardliners in support of US-China tough talk.
White House press secretary Karine Jean-Pierre told reporters Thursday that the U.S. will also consider taking broader action to expose and respond to China's larger-scale surveillance activities, which pose a threat to our national security and to our allies and partners.
The U.S. officials said they had notified the governments of more than 30 countries about the balloon incident and that international coordination was vital to counter the Chinese threat.
Senior researcher Emily Benson of the Center for Strategic and International Studies said that in addition to the actions of the Biden administration, the newly established U.S. House of Representatives U.S.-China Commission on Strategic Competition may pressure the United States to take more severe measures to slow down China's development.
She said that members of Congress would feel increasing pressure to take a more hardline stance, which could force the White House to take a more hardline stance.
The Wall Street Journal reported that many advocates of stricter export controls are also pushing to expand the scope of the controls to include artificial intelligence and other industries.
The US government is also in the process of developing an investment review plan to assess whether there are potential national security threats from China to its overseas investments.
Analysts say the White House may face pressure to move faster on the plan.
The first individual pension products have been launched, with minimum holding period of 360 days - Xinhua News Agency
The first individual pension products have been launched.
The 7 products offered by the home institution can be selected, with the shortest holding period being 360 days.
Personal pension investment products are finally available.
On February 10th, the China Wealth Management Network released the list of the first batch of individual pension product offerings from Industrial and Commercial Bank of China (ICBC), Agricultural Bank of China (ABC), and Postal Savings Bank of China (PSBC). Seven ICBC-managed individual pension products have officially launched.
At last, the “shelf” of personal pension accounts is complete with four products – personal pension savings, personal pension investment, personal pension insurance, and personal pension open-end funds.
According to the introduction, the first batch of individual pension funds will be all open-end mutual funds, of which 5 new products and 2 existing products will be launched. Among them, only one product is a mixed type product, and the other 6 products are fixed income type products.
The reporter of Beijing Youth Daily saw that 4 of the 5 new products were from ICBC Wealth Management, all of which were fixed-income products with the shortest holding period of 365 days, 540 days, 720 days and 1080 days, and the corresponding performance benchmarks (annualized) were 3.70% - 4.20%, 4.10% - 4.60%, 4.40% - 4.90% and 5.25% - 5.75%, respectively.
The remaining new product is "Post and Telecom Wealth Add Joy - Harmony Shortest Holding for 1095 Days No. 1", which is also a fixed-income product. It started fundraising on February 10th and ended on February 19th. The risk level is Level II.
Of the two products still in existence, one is Agricultural Bank of China's "Agricultural Bank of China Centennial - Dynamic" 360-day Innovation and Technology RMB Wealth Management Product with a mix investment nature and a risk level of three.
The second ongoing product is “Post and Express Wealth Add Joy - Harmony Shortest Holding for 365 Days No. 1,” which is of fixed income type. It started fundraising on December 30 last year and officially began operations on January 4 this year. Its cumulative net asset value as of February 8 was 1.0011.
According to the opinion of the State Council Office on Promoting the Development of Individual Pensions, the financial products in which the funds of the Individual Pension Fund Account can be invested include banking, savings deposits, commercial pension insurance, public funds, etc.
The first batch of individual pension fund management products was launched, marking that individual pension investors can officially purchase investment products through the individual pension fund account.
In November last year, the China Insurance Regulatory and Supervisory Commission formulated the “Interim Measures for the Management of Individual Pension Business of Commercial Banks and Wealth Management Companies”.
The Regulations provide that participants can purchase personal pension savings, personal pension wealth management products, personal pension insurance products, and personal pension open-end fund products through their individual pension funds accounts.
Subsequently, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security, the Ministry of Finance, and the State Administration of Taxation issued a notice to clarify that the individual pension plan will be implemented in 36 pilot cities and regions, including Beijing, Tianjin, and Hebei Shijiazhuang and the Xiongan New Area, Shanxi Jincheng City, and other cities and regions.
As of the end of 2022, the number of participants in the individual pension plan was 19.54 million, and the number of payers was 6.13 million, with a total amount of 14.2 billion yuan.
Previously, participating banks had only introduced three products for pilot testing: individual pension savings, individual pension insurance, and individual public offering funds.
Now that individual pension products have been aggregated, how should investors choose?
The expert of the product development department of CICC said that compared with other personal pension products, the pilot period of the pension products and the personal pension products have three characteristics.
The first is stability, better risk management mechanisms, more robust investment strategies and concepts, and the implementation of independent third-party custody outside the parent bank.
Second, long-term, the pilot phase of pension funds are valid for 5 years or more, and the next phase of the individual pension funds, the shortest holding period is one year, and it is encouraged to hold more than three years.
The third is accessibility, the product purchase threshold is low, the starting point is generally 1 yuan, some are as low as 0.01 yuan, the product handling fee, administration fee and other fees are more favorable.
Professionals point out that investors should choose products based on their characteristics and risk tolerance.
The personal pension savings have the characteristics of long period, high interest rate and high security, which are suitable for the people with low risk tolerance; the personal pension insurance products are more emphasis on protection, which are suitable for the people who cannot bear the investment risk and can accept the stable income; the personal pension investment products and public fund products are not guaranteed and not guaranteed the income, but the expected income is relatively high, which are suitable for the people with certain financial knowledge and high risk tolerance.
The article/Reporter of this newspaper, Chang-Yun, is published by the Chinese newspaper, Yue-Chang/Pike Haipo.
The Central Committee members, Standing Committee members and leading cadres of the provincial level or above learned the essence of Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress at the seminar on studying and implementing the essence of Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress - Rolling News - Hunan Daily - Huanxi
Newly-elected members of the Politburo Standing Committee and alternate members as well as provincial and ministerial-level leading cadres have completed their study course on implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China.
February 11, 2023 at 1:07 PM [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Sufeng] Font size: 【large | medium | small】
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 10 (covering the afternoon) - The study of the 20th CPC National Congress and the 20th CPC National Congress on the implementation of the new era of socialism with Chinese characteristics and the new members of the Central Committee, the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee, the leading cadres of the provincial-level departments and the leading cadres of the ministries and commissions attended the closing ceremony of the study of the implementation of the new era of socialism with Chinese characteristics and the 20th CPC National Congress in the Central Party School (the National Academy of Public Administration) on the 10th. Xi Jinping, a member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and the Secretary of the Central Secretariat of the CPC Central Committee, made a summary speech.
He said that he would thoroughly study and implement the important speech delivered by General Secretary Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar training class, with greater determination to uphold the “two establishments” and resolutely achieve the “two upholds,” strengthen his abilities and work hard to advance all tasks related to China’s modernization in accordance with the requirements of socialism with Chinese characteristics for a new era, and create achievements worthy of historical, practical, and people's judgment in fully building a modern socialist country and realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.
During the seminar, all the participants were guided by Xi Jinping's socialist ideas of China's new era, carefully studied the Party's spirit of the 20th and Xi Jinping's important speeches in the seminar, contacted practical in-depth research and exchange, deepened their understanding of a number of major theoretical and practical issues of Chinese modernization, strengthened their confidence and determination to promote the great rejuvenation of the Chinese people under the strong leadership of the Chinese Central Party, under the strong leadership of Comrade Xi Jinping, and strengthened their sense of responsibility and mission to fulfill their duties, do good work, and ensure a good start to the journey of the new era.
At the graduation ceremony, representatives from Class 10 made speeches to report and exchange their learning experiences.
Chai Qi stated that learning and implementing the thought of socialism with Chinese characteristics for a new era under Xi Jinping’s leadership is both an urgent political task for the present and in the future as well, and should be carried out according to the requirements of “comprehensive study, comprehensive grasp, and comprehensive implementation.” It is necessary to push forward the work on learning and implementing it further down deep, more solidly, and deeper into people's hearts.
To more deeply understand the decisive significance of “the two establishments,” we must resolutely uphold the core position of Xi Jinping and the authority of the Central Committee with Comrade Xi at its heart, as well as the centralized and unified leadership of the Party. We should continuously enhance our political judgment, political insight, and political execution, ensuring that we always maintain high consistency in thought, politics, and action with the Central Committee led by Comrade Xi.
To diligently master and apply Marxist theory as one’s forte, consciously arm oneself with the Party’s innovative theories to guide one’s thoughts, practice, and work, and strive to achieve deep study, meticulous understanding, and firm implementation in these areas; truly learn to acquire unwavering belief, absolute loyalty, and mission commitment.
To earnestly implement all decisions and deployments of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China with an enterprising spirit, advance the Chinese-style modernization, roll up our sleeves to work hard, get down to business as a good “construction supervisor”, step by step turn the blueprint into reality.
It is imperative to remember that comprehensive and strict governance of the Party must be pursued at all times, and self-revolution within the Party must also continue forever. The political responsibility for comprehensive and strict governance of the Party should be pressed firmly, with party political construction serving as the overarching principle, and efforts should be made to advance the new great project of Party building in the new era.
We should strengthen our ability to promote high-quality development, serve the people, and prevent and resolve risks, and promote the investigation and research spirit, resolutely prevent and overcome formalism and bureaucracy.
Stone Tiefeng, Li Ganjie, Li Shuyan, Chen Wenqing, Liu Jingguo, and Wang Xiaohong attended the graduation ceremony and Chen Xi presided over the graduation ceremony.
East Germany's last communist prime minister dies
The successor of the East German Communist Party, the Communist Party of Germany, reported in a statement that "Hans Modrow passed away last night at the age of 95".
Therefore, our party lost an important leader.
Translation requested.
On November 13, 1989, four days after the Berlin Wall was opened to reunite East and West Berlin, Modrow had said he would help turn East Germany into a democratic state.
At the time, the Communist Party leaders were forced to resign because of protests demanding democracy and freedom in the East.
After the Soviet Union came to power, Mikhail Gorbachev called for changes in Soviet-dominated Eastern Europe as well.
On March 1990, Modrow announced the first and only free election of the German Democratic Republic (GDR).
The election result led to his no longer being prime minister.
Despite Modr's reforms, opponents accused him of trying to delay the political change and unification that took place in October 1990.
He has also been criticized for trying to reform the secret police rather than abolish it.
In 1993, Modro was convicted of electoral fraud in the May 1989 municipal elections, but was not jailed.
Some have charged that these charges were motivated by political considerations.
From 1990 to 1994, Mörder continued to serve in the German parliament, and from 1999 to 2004 he was a member of the European Parliament.
Mr. Modro sees himself as a reformer and wants to change the Communist Party from within.
In 1999, he told Reuters that he did not want to see East Germany return, but said it should be acknowledged for its achievements.
Mordor was born in 1928 in the German town of Jasenitz (now Jasienica in Poland) and received training as a machinist.
During World War II, he served as a platoon leader in the Jungvolk, a youth organization of the Nazi Party, and later as a member of the Volkssturm, a Nazi organization that conscripted men aged 16 to 60 for the final war struggle.
At the age of 17, Modro was captured by the Soviet army and taken as a prisoner of war to the Soviet Union, where he attended an anti-fascist course and became a staunch Communist Party member.
In 1949, the year East Germany was founded, he returned to the country and found a job as a mechanical engineer and continued his studies in social sciences and economics, earning a doctorate.
Moderro was a staff member of the Free German Youth movement, which almost all East German youth joined, and was promoted to chairman of the Dresden regional party through the ruling Socialist Unity Party (SED) between 1973 and 1989.
He has also been a member of the East German parliament for more than 30 years.
In 1990, Moder became the de facto leader of East Germany, holding the highest state office.
VNA Hanoi - VNA correspondents reported that the official visit to Singapore and Brunei by Vietnamese Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh and his wife has been a complete success, yielding comprehensive, practical and specific results.
In the three days of his visit to Singapore and Brunei, Premier Feng Mingping attended more than 30 different events.
The results achieved have provided new impetus for the further development of the new strategic partnership between the two countries and the Vietnamese Comprehensive Partnership in a deeper, broader and more effective direction.
During his visit to the two countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh continued to reiterate the foreign policy of the Vietnamese Party and State, namely independence, diversity, flexibility, willingness to be a good friend and a reliable partner of all countries, and a responsible member of the international community.
Strengthening relations with Singapore and Brunei is in the interests of both countries, and is aimed at improving the well-being of their people, and at peace, stability and development in the region and the world.
At the meetings and talks, Pham Minh Chinh, Prime Minister, agreed with the leaders of Singapore and Brunei to continue to strengthen political trust with Vietnam through the high-level delegation visits, effective implementation of the various bilateral cooperation mechanisms and important cooperation agreements.
Many cooperation documents were signed during the visit.
Among these, two major highlights include the Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership signed with Singapore and the Action Plan for Strengthening Comprehensive Partnership between Vietnam and Brunei Darussalam for the 2023-2027 Period.
Vietnam and Singapore signed a Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership.
Image from the Vietnamese news agency
Vingroup President Nguyen Phu Trong stressed during meetings with business leaders, seminars or at economic forums that Vietnam is open to and ready to create favorable conditions for Singaporean and Bruneian companies to expand their investments in digital transformation, green energy, high-tech, innovation and creativity sectors in the country.
The visit will not only help deepen Vietnam's cooperation with Singapore and Brunei in traditional fields such as politics, diplomacy, economy, security, defence, education, training, oil and gas, tourism, people-to-people exchanges, but also create a framework for cooperation in new potential areas such as the digital economy, green economy, energy transition, innovation, smart cities, sustainable development.
King of Brunei Hassanal Bolkiah and Prime Minister of Viet Nam Pham Minh Chinh are preparing to enter the bilateral meeting.
Image from the Vietnamese news agency
During his visits to the two countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh arranged time to visit and listen to the thoughts and aspirations of the Vietnamese diaspora living in the two countries.
At the meeting with the leaders of the two countries, Pham Minh Chinh, Prime Minister of Vietnam, suggested that the authorities of both countries pay more attention to the fair treatment of the Vietnamese people in the host country, create conditions for the local Vietnamese community to contribute to the local society, and create favorable conditions for the development of bilateral relations.
The proposal has been agreed to and supported by both leaders of the two countries.
In particular, Prime Minister Fan Mingyi also shared with the leaders of the two countries the desire for a united, peaceful, stable and prosperous ASEAN community; agreed to maintain united cooperation with ASEAN countries and enhance the central role of ASEAN in the complex and changing context of regional and international situations.
Thanks to the important achievements, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh's official visit to Singapore and Brunei will contribute to effectively implementing the 13th National Congress of the Communist Party of Vietnam's guidelines on prioritizing relations with neighboring countries in the new context, effectively implementing the 12th conclusion of the Politburo of the Communist Party of Vietnam on the situation of Vietnamese overseas workers in the new context (12-KL/TW), and making positive contributions to the national solidarity force.
(Complete)
NEWS GOV-MO: Alert: Police Department urges citizens to be wary of fake text messages from telecom companies
The police in Japan have seized several cases of telecommunications fraud, where illegal actors faked the AstraZeneca company to send the owner of the scam text messages linked to the website, in order to get the points to be exchanged for a bribe as soon as possible, and to lure the owner to log in to a fake website for the exchange.
The victim inputted the card information and verification code as instructed and received a notification from the financial institution that there were unidentified transactions on the credit card. He suspected that his credit card information had been stolen from the website.
After verification, it was confirmed that the relevant telecommunication company did not send the above short message.
The Police Force appealed to the public to be vigilant if they received similar SMS messages, and not to click on the links or provide any personal information in the SMS; and to be extra careful if they were asked to provide credit card details, account transaction passwords and transaction verification codes, as they could be victims of credit card fraud.
Anti-fraud reminder:
1. Pay more attention to network security information, and improve personal prevention awareness.
2. Do not log in to websites with unknown origins and register your personal information and credit card information on the website, so as to avoid being stolen by others.
3. Be vigilant against fake websites and phishing websites, and always check that the website addresses are in full compliance with the official website;
4. Install antivirus software on phones, mobile devices, or computers and update it regularly;
If you suspect that you have been a victim of fraud or any other crime, please contact the Police Commissioner's Fraud Reporting Hotline at 8800 7777 or the Crime Report Line at 993 for assistance immediately.
EU summit debates refugee policy, EU officials: the process of reception is stalled - China News
EU summit on refugee policy: EU officials: bottlenecks at every step of the process
【Global Times reporter in Belgium, Ni Ruifeng】According to the report of the French news agency on February 10, at the latest EU summit held that day, the President of the European Commission, von der Leyen, said that the leaders of the EU agreed to issue stricter policies on illegal immigration to make it easier to expel illegal immigrants.
The EU's move is a response to the growing problem of illegal immigration in Europe, and now the core issue is that the number of illegal immigrants who can be deported is very small.
According to the summit document, EU leaders called on the Commission to immediately mobilize large amounts of EU funds to strengthen the external borders through infrastructure and surveillance.
Yet, there is bitter disagreement between the EU and its member states over payment of fence-related costs.
French Foreign Minister Alain Juppe said that the EU would not pay the costs.
But some diplomats from member countries said that if the EU could shoulder some of the cost of installing cameras, observation towers and other infrastructure along the external borders, it would free up national budgets to speed up construction.
EU officials acknowledge that the refugee reception process is blocked at every step, that the limited reception capacity and the overwhelming burden of the immigration authorities in the member states cannot stop refugees from filing their countless asylum applications in the EU countries, and that the EU's refugee reception system is in a near-permanent crisis state, according to the European website EURACTIV.
According to the European Commission, the number of asylum applications received by Schengen countries last year was more than 92,000, an increase of nearly half compared to the previous year.
Meanwhile, the EU recorded over 330,000 illegal entry cases last year.
In this context, the summit also agreed on a "principle" that EU member states can deport illegal immigrants to their home countries based on a court ruling of another member state.
In addition, the report said that the EU leaders also agreed to "increase the use of the concept of security countries," which will pave the way for the EU to draw up a common list.
(Source: Global Times; Author: Liu Ruifei)
Hsia Liuyan, vice chairman of the Kuomintang, conveyed Song Tao’s message that the 1992 Consensus is welcome for Green camp visits to China.
Taiwan China Nationalist Party Vice Chairman Xia Liuyan met with both the State Councilor and Premier of the People's Republic of China, Wang Linqing, and the Director-General of the Office of the Central People’s Government in the Taiwan Area, Song Tao, on separate occasions this time.
Senior Advisor Zhao Chunshan of the Nationalist Party’s official organization, the Council for Political and Economic Affairs, yesterday evening accepted an interview with Taiwan’s Central News Agency and actively praised Song Tao’s comments on Xia Liuyan that as long as one agrees to “the 92 Consensus” and anti-Taiwanese independence, China welcomes Green camp figures to visit mainland China.
The KMT side evaluated it as a new thing.
Xia Liyan met with Song Tao earlier that day, but the news did not mention this claim.
The ruling Democratic Progressive Party in Taiwan has repeatedly denied accepting the "92 Consensus".
According to Central News Agency, the Central Committee of the Kuomintang (KMT) led by Vice Chairman Shieh Liang-ying visited China and met with the Politburo member of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China (CPC) Wang Hongbing, the new head of the Taiwanese Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee, and the Party Secretary of Beijing City Committee, Yan Q everybody.
Xia Liying and Song Tao met to discuss the political foundation of the CPC and the anti-Taiwan independence, and Zhao Chunshan, a senior advisor of the Nationalist Party, said that the "92 Consensus" of the Nationalist Party was the original "92 Consensus".
Zhao Chunshan notes that this is different from his previous experiences at meetings.
Recently, I had a video conference with scholars from the mainland, and this time, I did not hear any scholars talking about the unification and the “anti-secession law”. Instead, I heard the restoration of exchanges and dialogues.
Zhao Chunshan pointed out that the cross-strait situation is tense and dangerous, and the mainland hopes to convey the intention of improving relations through the Kuomintang.
Because there is no mutual trust between the two sides, the other party still wants to do a good job for the Taiwanese, and the representative does not want to make the cross-strait relations worse.
According to Liu Chunsan, Wang Liening personally instructed Liu to tell them about their demands (Taiwanese farmers and fishermen) that you must implement the demands, and if you cannot resolve them, you will have to deal with them on a case-by-case basis.
The report did not mention whether the KMT delegation mentioned the Chinese military aircraft and naval ships that intrude into Taiwan every day, the problems of farming and fishing in some counties and cities in Taiwan, and whether the Central News Agency reporters asked such questions.
What was the mysterious object that crashed in Alaska's airspace?
Confusing and contradictory, speculation rife.
The U.S. military used its most advanced stealth fighter, the F-22, to shoot down an unidentified object flying in the air above Alaska on Friday afternoon.
The location is about 10 miles off the coast of Alaska.
This is the second time in less than a week that the U.S. military has shot down an unidentified flying object.
A Chinese spy balloon was shot down over the US coast of South Carolina on Saturday, days after it was floating over US airspace.
The Pentagon said the second object, which first entered U.S. airspace on Thursday night, was tracked by the U.S. military as it moved over northeastern Alaska, flying at an altitude of 12,000 meters (40,000 feet), was about the size of a small car and much smaller than the Chinese spy balloon that was shot down earlier.
The Pentagon also believes that there is no indication that the object is currently capable of being manipulated.
John Coby, White House National Security Council strategic communications coordinator, said Friday that while the exact nature of the object flying high in the sky is not clear, it poses a legitimate threat to the safety of civil aviation aircraft.
According to Kobe, the object is different from the spy balloon found in the United States, as it does not have a suspended canister of a payload.
Kobe said, "We call it a 'thing' because that's the best description we can make of it right now."
President Biden listened to the Pentagon's advice before ordering the object to be shot down, and he was very cautious in making the decision, Corby added.
The official description of the object in the United States can be roughly summarized as: It was the size of a small car, without a handlebar, no suspension, and was flying at an altitude of about 10,000 meters.
But these data do not answer basic questions such as what this object is, which country it belongs to, and what mission it is performing.
Currently, much of the analysis and speculation online suggests that this may be another Chinese balloon.
It could be from China, like the spy balloon that invaded US airspace and the Chinese balloon that was hovering over Latin America, both of which are performing a mission in different locations.
Some have even linked the Alaska "object" to the mysterious flying object (UFO).
The report in the US News & World Report cites former US Congressman Peter Meijer’s tweet on Friday that he hopes this “unidentified flying object” is an espionage balloon rather than a legitimate UFO.
The irony of Liu confusing alien spacecraft with weather balloons is surprising, but it doesn't deserve to trigger an interstellar conflict, Liu Meijer said.
The tweet was posted shortly after Kobe confirmed that the object in Alaska had been shot down.
The newsweekly said that Major was not the only one to suspect the object of being a UFO.
Republican Tennessee Representative Tim Burchett criticized the government's cover-up of information last month, demanding the Director of National Intelligence (DNI) release a report on "unidentified flying objects."
Xi Jinping's Letter to the Members of the Chinese Medical Team in Africa Encourages Them to Practice Compassionate Medicine to Benefit the Local People and to Tell the Story of China with Real Actions - News - Hunan Daily - Huanxi Shibao
Xi Jinping's Letter to the Medical Team of China-Africa Friendship Hospital Encourages the Team Members to Practice Compassionate Medicine and Tell the Story of China with Real Actions
February 11, 2023 at 1:09 PM [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Sufeng] Font size: 【large medium small】
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 10 - General Secretary of the CPC Central Committee, President of the People's Republic of China and Chairman of the Central Military Commission Xi Jinping sent a letter to the 19th batch of medical team to the Central African Republic on February 9, expressing his greetings to them and all the medical teams abroad and making a sincere wish.
In his reply, Xi Jinping said that you have overcome difficulties in work and life in the Central African Republic, and have served the local people with your heart, and you are both a white angel of rescue and a friendly ambassador.
This year is the 60th anniversary of the dispatch of the Chinese medical team. I sincerely express my gratitude to the comrades who are currently and have ever carried out the medical mission abroad.
Xi Jinping pointed out that the Chinese people love peace and cherish life, and medical aid is a vivid embodiment of this.
I hope you will not forget your first thoughts, remember your mission, and work hard to promote the spirit of the Chinese medical team, which is dedicated to sacrifice, rescue and relief, and loves no borders, to benefit the local people with kindness and charity, to tell the story of China with practical actions, and to make a greater contribution to promoting the construction of a community of human health and health.
Foreign medical aid is an important content of China’s foreign aid work.
In 1963, the first medical support team was sent to Algeria.
Over the past 60 years, the company has sent 30,000 medical teams to 76 countries and regions in Africa, Asia, the Americas, Europe and Oceania, and treated 290 million patients, earning wide praise from the international community.
Currently, the medical teams are working in 115 medical facilities in 56 countries around the world, with almost half of them in remote and difficult areas.
Recently, 11 members of the 19th batch of China’s medical teams dispatched to Central Africa wrote letters to President Xi Jinping, reporting on their efforts in implementing the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress and providing medical services for local residents, as well as expressing their determination to contribute to building a community with a shared future for mankind.
Iranian revolution anniversary: Hacker supporting protests hijacks presidential speech
An official rally was held on Saturday to mark the 44th anniversary of the Islamic Revolution in Iran, but an anti-government hacker briefly interrupted a televised speech by President Ibrahim Raisi.
The president's televised address was interrupted for about a minute on the internet, and a screen appeared with the symbol of the Iranian hackers group "Edalat Ali" (Ali's Justice).
The voice of the Muslim Brotherhood in the country was also heard shouting "Death to the Islamic Republic".
According to Reuters, hackers disrupted the broadcast of the state television on the anniversary of the Iranian Revolution.
The Iranian authorities mark the 44th anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, and while the hardline government of Reiss faces the biggest challenge yet from young protesters demanding their removal, Reiss still calls on the deceived youth to repent so that they can be pardoned by Iran's supreme leader.
The wave of nationwide protests continues in Iran after the death of 22-year-old Mahsa Amini in September in the custody of the country's moral police.
The deadly crackdown on protests by Iranian security forces is one of the biggest challenges facing the Islamic Republic since the 1979 revolution that toppled the 2,500-year-old monarchy.
As part of an amnesty in celebration of the anniversary of the revolution, Iranian authorities freed Friday two political prisoners who had been on hunger strike: Farkhaddin Mesbah-Yazdi and Fariba Adel-Haeri, an Iranian-French scholar.
Earlier, Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei issued an amnesty for some prisoners arrested during recent anti-government protests.
According to the report of Human Rights Activists Network (HRANA), as of Friday, 528 protesters have been killed, including 71 minors.
The report said that 70 other government security personnel were killed.
It is believed that up to 19,763 protesters were arrested.
For weeks, Iranian leaders and state media have been calling for a vote at Saturday's rally to show opposition to the protests and support for the government.
On the eve of the anniversary of the Iranian revolution on Friday night, state media showed fireworks as part of a government-sponsored celebration, with people chanting "Allahu Akbar!"
(God is the greatest!)
However, many people at the rally were also heard shouting "Death to the dictator!"
The video of the death of the Islamic Republic of Iran in the city of Qamishli, in the south of the country, was posted on social media.
Saturday, the government television station aired footage of the official meetings of the various states.
In Tehran, as part of the official celebrations, domestic anti-ballistic missiles, drones, anti-submarine cruisers and other military equipment were displayed.
President Lacey's speeches are often interrupted by the slogan "Fire to America", a signature slogan at state rallies.
The crowd chanted "Israel must die."
Adelkhah, who has been in prison since 2019, is one of seven French nationals detained in Iran, Reuters said, a factor in the deterioration of relations between Paris and Tehran in recent months.
She was sentenced to five years in prison in 2020 on charges of national security.
They later placed her under house arrest, but she was returned to jail in January.
Adelkhah denies the accusations.
A week before Mesami was released, supporters warned that he was in danger of death as a result of the hunger strike.
He was arrested in 2018 for protesting the mandatory wearing of headscarves.
The French Foreign Ministry responded to Adelkhah's release on Friday, calling for her freedom to be restored, including the possibility of her being allowed to return to France if she wishes.
Translation requested.
The 16th China-Japan Energy Saving and Environmental Protection Comprehensive Forum was held in Beijing. He Lifeng attended the main forum and delivered a keynote speech - China News
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 11 - The 16th China-Japan Energy Saving and Environmental Protection Comprehensive Forum was held in Beijing on the 11th of February with a combination of online and offline ways.
Hu Lifeng, member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Central Committee and Director of the National Development and Reform Commission, delivered a keynote speech at the main forum.
Huang Lifeng noted that hosting this forum is an important step in implementing the consensus reached at the joint meeting between President Xi Jinping and Prime Minister Fumio Kishida in Bangkok to strengthen green development cooperation between China and Japan.
China will fully implement the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress, accelerate the green transformation of development, deepen the prevention and control of environmental pollution, comprehensively strengthen resource conservation, actively and steadily promote carbon peaking and carbon neutrality, promote the coordinated reduction of carbon, pollution, greening, and growth, and promote ecological priority, resource conservation, and low-carbon, green development.
China is willing to work with Japan to deepen green and low-carbon industry cooperation, technology cooperation, policy dialogue and cultural exchange, and promote the development of green cooperation between the two countries to a new level.
Japanese Minister of Economy, Trade and Industry Shunji Watanabe attended the main forum and delivered a keynote speech.
The forum was jointly hosted by the National Development and Reform Commission, Ministry of Commerce of China and the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry of Japan, and the Japan Chamber of Commerce and Industry. It included a main forum and four sub-forums, namely, energy efficiency improvement, automobile electrification, smart automobile, hydrogen energy, and long-term trade between China and Japan.
Representatives from the governments, enterprises and institutions of both China and Japan attended the exchange.
Q&A on Double Ninth Festival | How to Interpret the Unexpectedly Strong Non-Farm Payrolls Data in January and Its Future Trends - Economic Observer - A Professional Financial News Website
Q: How do you see the January non-farm employment data in the US going beyond expectations and future trends?
A: On February 3, the US Department of Labor released the employment data of non-agricultural employment in January 2023. The number of new non-agricultural employment was 517,000, which was much higher than the market expectations of 189,000; the unemployment rate fell to 3.4%, which was the lowest level in the past 50 years; the average hourly wage growth was 4.4%, which was slightly slower than the previous month.
From a total perspective, this data is subject to many one-off and technical factors of disturbance, such as teachers returning from strike, adjustments in survey statistics, updates on seasonal adjustment factors, etc., which may be revised (refer to the downward revision of non-farm payroll employment for January 2022 from 5.04 million to 3.64 million). Non-farm payroll employment may not be as strong as it appears in the data.
From the perspective of structure, the layoff impact of high-tech enterprises is still there, but the proportion is relatively low; the employment of high-contact service industries such as leisure hotels, education and health care has increased significantly, and the labor shortage of the service industry is still there.
Combined with the same strong service PMI, job vacancies and labor shortage data, and the strong credit data of consumer spending, we judged that the US service industry recovered rapidly after extreme weather and holidays.
We believe that the tightness of the U.S. labor market will not improve without a recession.
At present, the supply gap of the US labor market is still more than 5 million, and the labor participation rate is rising slowly, especially the labor participation rate of 25-54-year-olds has reached the peak before the epidemic.
Moreover, because of strong excess saving and consumption credit among US residents, the strength of consumer demand will further delay the impact on employment markets from tightening policies.
The tight labor market in the US will be the bottom color of the US economy in 2023.
The combination of the near-ending of the tightening cycle and the repeated fluctuation of inflation expectations is not optimistic about the continuous decline of wage growth.
Prior to the release of the data, the US stock, bond and foreign exchange markets were overly optimistic about the path of interest rate hikes by the Federal Reserve.
With the continuing improvement in inflation data, the Fed has continued to maintain the fragile balance of market inflation expectations while shortening the pace of rate hikes, but the market has ignored the Fed's biased rhetoric, not only expecting an early halt in rate hikes, but also two rate cuts by the end of the year.
In the context of tight labour market supply and demand and uncertain effects of austerity policy, we believe that the Fed's guidance for interest rate hikes at the end of the year is relatively reasonable, and that the extreme market expectations of adjustment and trade congestion will cause some damage to the market.
Nevertheless, the stiffness of wage growth is difficult to change the current trend of rapid decline in inflation, as the year-on-year turnover of M2 data and the gradual improvement of the leading indicators of various CPI scores, the US CPI data has moved to a rapid decline since October, the stiffness of wage growth will only form a basis for future inflation data, the current market expectations are difficult to falsify, the next round of inflation data is published in the market or enter a new round of games.
Shenzhen: Building the first and leading city of extreme speed pioneers in China - China News Service
China News Service, February 11 - According to the "Shenzhen Industry and Information" WeChat public number, the Shenzhen Municipal Industry and Information Bureau recently issued the "Shenzhen Action Plan for the Construction of the Ultra-Fast City".
It is proposed that by the end of 2023, a super broadband network with high rates, large capacity, and low latency will be built to achieve the goal of “Dual Gigabit, Full Optical Network, 1 millisecond, Everything Connected,” making it China’s first and world-leading city in terms of ultra-fast speed.
The plan calls for accelerating the upgrade of the gigabit optical network.
By the end of 2023, the proportion of 10G PON ports will reach 100%, and the number of full-light industrial parks (industrial parks) will exceed 100.
The plan requires that the efficiency of 5G networks be improved.
The research will be conducted to develop the 5G network service quality standards in Shenzhen, conduct 5G network test and evaluation, and improve the quality of 5G network services.
Support the operators of basic telecommunications to increase the optimization of 5G networks in key areas and places, and add 10,000 5G base stations throughout the year. The average download speed in the city will reach 500 Mbps, and the upload speed will reach 100 Mbps. The download speed in key areas will reach 1 Gbps, and the upload speed will reach 200 Mbps. The network speed and user experience will be greatly improved.
The project aims to build a high-quality wireless local area network at the city level.
To establish a standard for public WLAN services, to promote the upgrade of WLAN in areas with dense population and information consumption needs in all districts of the city, and to provide 1000Mbps access capability.
By leveraging the "Shen i net", the city has built a unified authentication and management platform for public wireless local area networks, which supports "one-time authentication, roaming without awareness, and intelligent switching". The platform supports the operation entities to include the APs (access points) with public service capabilities in the authentication and management platform.
By the end of 2023, the total number of upgraded access APs will be at least 20,000.
In addition, the plan also proposes to build a high-quality all-photovoltaic power network, build a multi-level power supply system, accelerate the construction of critical communications network facilities, and improve the Internet application service capability.
The plan clearly states that collaborative construction of an IoT perception system will be carried out.
Explore the construction of a management model for the construction of urban perception terminals based on the open source XIMON OS, reduce the linkage costs, accelerate the construction of city-level IoT perception platforms, promote the interconnection of IoT platforms in cities, specialized IoT platforms in various fields.
Deepen application of IoT perception in urban management, public services, public safety, and traffic travel, expand fixed sensing channels such as city roads, buildings, and public facilities, and mobile sensing channels such as intelligent connected vehicles.
By the end of 2023, more than 9 million water, electricity, and gas IoT sensing terminals will be deployed, with the aim to launch 20 demonstration projects for multi-functional smart poles.
The plan also includes strengthening the integration of satellite and ground communications, building low-level network infrastructure, and advancing deep coverage of 5G networks at sea.
At the same time, it will promote the in-depth coverage of 5G network in the sea, build an innovation development ecological environment for the industry, and support the top-level events and activities.
(Cai News Finance)
China’s e-commerce industry is emerging with a “new variable”, how to do live broadcasting in a way that is “content-oriented”?
China News Service
China News Service, February 11 - The Chinese e-commerce industry has emerged a "new variable", how to do "content is king" to promote?
Xia Bin, a reporter from China Finance News
We entered the e-commerce business late, but we realized from the beginning that to stand out in the sea of millions of stores, content is very important.
Fangfang, an 90s girl from Guangdong who runs a health food store on Douyin e-commerce, has made her offline business that has been around for over three decades blossom online.
The video is beautiful and refreshing. The video is a copy of the old Hong Kong movie, with classic Chinese songs, and the video opens the @fangfang account and eats the same old Hong Kong song.
At the recent Xiong'an e-commerce forum for the search for peers and sharing of quality content, Fangfang spoke as a representative of quality creators, presenting his experiences and experiences of daily creation.
She said on stage: "The carefully polished video has attracted much attention from netizens, and many people are interested in my family's ingredients, wanting to make their own food together; sales have opened up immediately."
Translation requested.
Fang Fang used to make videos of cooking soup to make more people love the taste of "old Guangzhou", and sold 300,000 units of nourishing food in a single live broadcast, saving the old store that was on the verge of bankruptcy.
“No content, no e-commerce”, as short videos and live broadcast e-commerce continue to develop, people’s requirements and standards for e-commerce content are entering a new stage.
In the early days of live broadcasting, the station often used low discounts to attract users, and the price advantage seemed to be the only selling point at the time.
In recent years, there have been many phenomenal KOLs, such as Liu Liang Hong and Fan Jia Yuan, as well as many non-mainstream KOLs and merchants who have emerged in the vertical field. They have continuously created high-quality content that matches their brand characteristics, and have improved their long-term operating efficiency.
Gao Yaxuan, the head of the operation of the star author of the video e-commerce of Douyin, introduced that in the past year, 6.27 million creators have turned their content into income through Douyin video e-commerce, and their content creation volume has increased by 252%, and the total sales amount has increased by more than 100%.
Behind these numbers, we can feel a vibrant, growing author ecosystem with a lot of vitality.
Gao Yaxuan said.
The Beijing Normal University Platform for Innovation in Communication and Future Media previously released the ECHI Report on the Content Ecological Health Index of the E-commerce Industry, which analyzed the importance of high-quality content from a data perspective, assessing the content ecological status of 27 major e-commerce platforms domestically using an index system.
According to the report on the health index of the e-commerce industry, TikTok, Kuaishou, Taobao, Pinduoduo, and JD.com ranked in the top five.
The report believes that the e-commerce industry content ecology is a comprehensive concept, which integrates e-commerce and content, but not all content can be integrated with e-commerce. The best PGC (professional production of content) and UGC (user-generated content) are the carriers for the integration of e-commerce and content, and the value of the content platform is higher, the consumption and promotion scenarios are more and more rich, and the possibility of e-commerce integration is also higher, and the commercial value is also stronger. The proportion of public and private integration of e-commerce content production and consumption will gradually increase.
On-site, Professor Yu Guoming of Beijing Normal University’s School of Journalism and Communication, who is also chairman of the China Media Economics and Management Professional Committee, provided an analysis and interpretation of the report.
He said that in terms of content value, the current e-commerce industry has transitioned from “accessibility to consumption” to “quality-oriented consumption,” and high-quality, professional, and differentiated content is the “hard currency” of the e-commerce industry.
At the same time, content becomes the fundamental and the handle for the new stage of e-commerce development. PGC (Professional Generated Content) content such as knowledge payment, professional knowledge, KOL (Key Opinion Leader) and so on becomes the standard in e-commerce live broadcast.
Looking ahead to the future development of the e-commerce industry, Yu Guomin put forward two suggestions.
One is to promote the overall improvement of the ecological health of e-commerce content and quality from the perspective of improving the content structure, to create positive content creation and management standards, and to achieve the index of the e-commerce industry's content ecological health system and dynamic balance.
Another one is from the external ecological perspective, to achieve the healthy development of the content e-commerce industry and the value co-creation and co-prosperity with the external environment.
In the future, the e-commerce industry needs more data and artificial intelligence support to predict the stability of the future development; in addition, it needs to provide more standardized and healthy growth space for merchants to realize the value cooperation of enterprises, users, products and services, and create a healthy content ecology.
"(" (complete)
The Biden administration added six Chinese entities to the blacklist on Friday (February 10) for their alleged involvement in the suspected spy balloon program.
The U.S. Department of Commerce said the five Chinese companies and one research institution helped modernize the Chinese military, especially in the aviation and aerospace projects, including flying boats and aircraft.
Companies on the blacklist have difficulty obtaining US technology exports.
The list is called the Entity List, and companies on the list will not be able to purchase technology or goods from U.S. suppliers unless they have received a special export license from the U.S. Department of Commerce.
The companies listed on the blacklist are: Beijing Nanjiang Sky Space Technology Co., Ltd., China Electronics Science and Technology Group Fourth Eighth Research Institute, Dongguan Lingkong Remote Sensing Technology Co., Ltd., Eagle Gate Aviation Technology Group Co., Ltd., Guangzhou Tianhai Xiang Aeronautical Technology Co., Ltd., and Shanxi Eagle Gate Aviation Technology Group Co., Ltd.
Prior to this, the White House said it was considering more sweeping measures to "expose and address" China's broader surveillance activities that threaten U.S. national security.
The balloon incident has further strained relations between China and the United States, and US Secretary of State Blinken has canceled his visit to China.
China's government expressed its solemn representations to the US embassy in China on February 4 after the US shot down the balloon, criticizing the US for seriously damaging and undermining the efforts and progress of stabilizing China-US relations.
Based on the existing debris evidence and information from the Chinese military procurement platform, the US government concluded that the manufacturer of the balloon was "directly related to the Chinese People's Liberation Army" and was an approved supplier of the Chinese military.
Mao Ning, spokesperson of the Chinese Foreign Ministry, said at the news conference on Friday that the Chinese side had repeatedly explained the situation and position on the accident of the unmanned Chinese aircraft entering the US airspace due to force majeure.
According to the State Department website, she added that the relevant US congressional resolution is purely political manipulation and hype.
China is strongly dissatisfied and resolutely opposes this.
Matthew Axelrod, Assistant Secretary of Commerce for Export Enforcement, said: "Today's action demonstrates our collective efforts to identify and prevent China from using spy balloons that violate the airspace of the United States and more than 40 countries".
Translation requested.
Reuters reports that an employee of Tianhaixiang Aviation Technology Co., Ltd. in Guangzhou said he was not aware of the sanctions and declined further comment.
China's embassy in the United States and the Chinese Foreign Ministry have not commented on the information.
(Reuters et al.)
