The product is good, but Amazon's after-sales service is really worse than other websites
After placing the order, I found that I had made a mistake, but I couldn't cancel the order. The error page of the online customer service showed an error link, and I couldn't contact it.
After receiving the goods, the delivery man called me and I said I didn't want it, but the cancellation of the order was not successful, and the delivery man took it back, saying that I should sign for it first, and then I could apply for a return.
The only thing that is said when you request a refund is that the food category cannot be returned once the order is received, and there is no way to call Amazon customer service, which is the same as saying that the order cannot be returned.
I have bought non-returnable items on JD.com and Suning before, including milk and diapers, and contacted the customer service to get them returned. The diapers opened after they were delivered smelled too bad, but the customer service still gave me a refund. On Amazon, you can't get a refund for non-returnable items.
The rules are dead, people are alive, how should we handle this? Contact our customer service department.
Either I take it myself or I let the delivery person buy it, the delivery person is already hard enough, why should I make them spend money to buy something that is not theirs?
I'm not going to back down, I'm going to take it myself, but I have to give you a credit for your service.
Headphone distortion, and noise
